carlos-emr (2026.09.0~snapshot4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Default rename: the database is now `carlos` (was the inherited `oscar`)
    and the document store is now CarlosDocument (was OscarDocument), with a
    `carlos` instance segment: /var/lib/carlos-emr/CarlosDocument/carlos.
  * One-time migrations, applied only when upgrading from before this version
    and only where the OLD STOCK DEFAULT is still in effect — an explicitly
    configured CARLOS_DB_NAME or a post-upgrade OscarDocument directory is
    never touched:
    - the `oscar` schema is renamed to `carlos` in place via the new
      idempotent `carlos-ctl db-rename-schema` (atomic multi-pair RENAME
      TABLE; flyway_schema_history and its checksums move unchanged), then
      CARLOS_DB_NAME / CARLOS_BACKUP_DB_NAME are updated. If MariaDB is down
      the rename defers to the next configure (dpkg-reconfigure carlos-emr).
    - the document store is moved to CarlosDocument with an OscarDocument
      compat symlink left behind, so absolute paths already stored in the
      database (faxes, email attachments) keep resolving.
  * The weekly restore drill accepts both directory spellings: the newest
    snapshot right after the upgrade still carries pre-rename paths.
  * Upgrades no longer leave the EMR down behind a 502. carlos-emr,
    carlos-emr-drugref and carlos-emr-eform-renderer each restart
    carlos-emr.service, so one apt transaction restarts it three times; against
    the unit's StartLimitBurst=6/30min an install followed by an upgrade inside
    the same half hour exhausted the budget and systemd refused the last restart
    with "start-limit-hit". Package-driven restarts — and `carlos-ctl
    start`/`restart` — now clear the start counter first, and the two dependent
    postinsts recover a unit an earlier one in the same transaction left failed.
    Crash-loop protection is unchanged: Restart=on-failure with RestartSec=15s
    still trips the same limit in about 90 seconds.

 -- CARLOS EMR Maintainers <michael@maplecreekmedical.ca>  Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0000

carlos-emr (2026.09.0~snapshot3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Install wizard: recommend a Java heap sized from the machine's memory
    instead of a static 2g — half of physical RAM, rounded to the nearest GB,
    clamped to 2g..8g — as the pre-filled answer to the java-heap question on
    first install (successor to the OSCAR-19 packaging's 60%-of-RAM sizing).
    Preseeded, reconfigured and upgraded installs keep their existing answer.

