carlos-emr (2026.09.0~snapshot2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Fix nine clinician-facing bugs reported by alpha testers on the .deb
    deployment (only reproducible through the nginx + ModSecurity front door):
    Rx staging (Hibernate 7 HQL "order by drugid" regression), pharmacy
    "Return to RX", messenger group admin (missing jQuery core + selectors),
    eChart history 403 and document-upload 400 (WAF clinical-workflow
    exclusions), X-ray incoming-doc blank iframe, consultation signatures, and
    the Consultations tab dropping provider-orphaned rows.
  * WAF: ship package-managed per-route clinical exclusions (ids 1000-1999) and
    operator-owned local-exclusions-{before,after}-crs.conf (ids 5000-5999);
    document the carlos-ctl waf tail -> exclude -> reload -> check workflow.
  * Enable consultation signatures by default, with a one-time upgrade migration
    that flips the old stock consultation_signature_enabled=false to true while
    preserving an operator's explicit choice.
  * Packaging: reload systemd on upgrade before restarting carlos-emr so a
    changed unit file takes effect without a manual daemon-reload; on purge,
    remove the generated carlos-emr.env and the consultation-signature migration
    sentinel so a later reinstall is genuinely fresh (province/timezone answers
    are honoured again); guard the debconf db_get calls against set -e; stop
    resetting an operator-diverged CARLOS_JAVA_XMS back to Xmx on upgrade;
    document the deb pre-release version ladder in README.source (a ~rc after
    a shipped ~snapshot would sort as a downgrade).

